%% Fact Book section for Topic 7 — included by content/FB/main.gsm under a "Topic 7" H1.

## T7 · Dates and milestones

::: table | Topic 7 timeline — laws, theories, cases and the three case studies.
@widths 1.8,12.2
@font 9.5
Year | Event
1860 | Pakistan (Indian) Penal Code — s. 509 insult to modesty
1961 | Bandura's Bobo doll experiments
1969 | Galtung defines structural violence
1971 | Goode's resource theory of family violence
1973 | Bandura, *Aggression: A Social Learning Analysis*
1975 | Brownmiller, *Against Our Will*
1976 | Dowry and Bridal Gifts (Restriction) Act
1978 | Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy born in Karachi
1979 | Hudood Ordinances (Zina); Dobash and Dobash, *Violence Against Wives*; Walker, *The Battered Woman*; CEDAW
1981 | Duluth Domestic Abuse Intervention Project — Power and Control Wheel
1987 | Connell, *Gender and Power*; Kaufman's triad of men's violence
1988 | Kelly, *Surviving Sexual Violence* — the continuum
1990 | Qisas and Diyat Ordinance (Act 1997); Galtung, "Cultural Violence"
1992 | CEDAW General Recommendation 19
1993 | Vienna Conference; DEVAW (20 December)
1994 | Women's police stations in Pakistan; UN Special Rapporteur on VAW
1995 | Beijing Platform — Critical Area D; Connell, *Masculinities*
1996 | Pakistan accedes to CEDAW
1997 | Malala born (12 July, Mingora)
1998 | Heise's ecological model; Rozan founded
1999 | 25 November named International Day for the Elimination of VAW; Samia Sarwar killed
2000 | NCSW; UNSCR 1325
2002 | Mukhtaran Mai gang-raped (22 June, Meerwala); ATC sentences six (August); National Policy for Development and Empowerment of Women
2004 | Criminal Law (Amendment) Act — honour crimes defined; *Saima Waheed* (SC)
2005 | LHC acquits five in the Mukhtaran Mai case
2006 | Protection of Women (Criminal Laws Amendment) Act; *In the Name of Honor*
2007 | Stark, *Coercive Control*; Taliban control Swat
2009 | Malala's BBC Urdu diary ("Gul Makai")
2010 | Workplace harassment Act; s. 509 amended; ICCPR and CAT ratified
2011 | Acid Control Act; Anti-Women Practices Act; SC upholds Mukhtaran Mai acquittals (21 April); Istanbul Convention
2012 | *Saving Face* wins the Oscar; Malala shot (9 October); NCSW Act
2013 | Sindh DV Act; Sindh child-marriage law (18); Malala's UN speech (12 July); *I Am Malala*; Malala Fund
2014 | Balochistan DV Act; Malala's Nobel Peace Prize (10 December); Saba Qaiser shot; "I am not Malala" day; Sughra Imam's honour bill
2015 | SDG 5.2 and 5.3
2016 | *A Girl in the River* wins the Oscar (February); Punjab Protection of Women against Violence Act (24 February); Qandeel Baloch killed (July); honour-killing Act and anti-rape Act (October); PECA
2017 | VAWC Multan; Punjab Women Protection Authority; CEDAW GR 35
2018 | Zainab Ansari murdered (Kasur, January); Trafficking in Persons Act; Transgender Persons Act
2020 | Zainab Alert Act; motorway gang rape (September)
2021 | Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act (1 December); KP DV Act; Noor Mukadam murdered
2022 | Harassment Act amended; LHC acquits Qandeel Baloch's brother
2025 | Malala at Islamabad girls' education conference (January); SC upholds Noor Mukadam verdict (May); Sana Yousaf killed (2 June); Degari killings; ICT child-marriage and DV Acts
:::

## T7 · Figures

::: table | Figures used in Topic 7.
@widths 6.5,3,4.5
@font 9.5
Figure | Value | Source (year)
Women experiencing physical or sexual violence worldwide | about 1 in 3 (≈736 million) | WHO (2021)
Women and girls killed intentionally worldwide | about 85,000 | UNODC/UN Women (2023)
Killed by partners or family | about 51,100 — one every 10 minutes | UNODC/UN Women (2023)
Ever-married women: physical violence since 15 | 28% | PDHS (2017–18)
Ever-married women: spousal physical, sexual or emotional violence | 34% | PDHS (2017–18)
Survivors who never sought help | 56% | PDHS (2017–18)
Reported GBV cases | 32,617 | SSDO (2024)
Rape / kidnapping / DV / honour killing cases | 5,339 / 24,439 / 2,238 / 547 | SSDO (2024)
Conviction rates | rape 0.5%; honour 0.5%; DV 1.3%; kidnapping 0.1% | SSDO (2024)
Honour killings | at least 405 | HRCP (2024)
Honour killings (latest) | at least 470; 1,332 domestic-violence murders | HRCP (2025; report May 2026)
Cases of violence against women and girls documented | 14,425 | HRCP (2024)
Acid attack punishment | 14 years to life; fine ≥ Rs 1 million | Acid Act 2011
Punjab Act: decision time | 90 days (first hearing within 7) | 2016
Punjab Act: breach of order | up to 1 year (repeat 1–2 years) | 2016
Malala Fund investment in Pakistan | about $14.6 million since 2013 | Malala Fund (2025)
Out-of-school children in Pakistan | more than 25 million | —
Past MCQs on Topic 7 | 12 of 140 | CSS record (2016–2026)
:::

## T7 · Key comparisons

::: table | Comparisons examiners like in Topic 7.
@widths 3.4,5.3,5.3
@font 9.5
Aspect | One side | The other side
GBV vs VAW | Violence because of gender — any person | Violence against women (DEVAW 1993)
Direct vs structural violence | A perpetrator harms a victim | Harm built into structures (Galtung 1969)
Cycle of violence vs power and control | Repeating phases: tension, explosion, contrition (Walker 1979) | Tactics of control held together by violence (Duluth 1981)
Intimate terrorism vs situational couple violence | Pattern of control, mostly men | Conflicts that escalate, both sexes (Johnson)
2004 vs 2016 honour law | Defined honour crimes; pardons still possible | Life imprisonment even after forgiveness
Saving Face vs A Girl in the River | Acid attacks; Oscar 2012; Acid Act 2011 | Honour killing; Oscar 2016; honour Act 2016
Protection order vs residence order | Keeps the abuser away (no contact, GPS) | Secures the woman's home or shelter
Root cause vs trigger | Why violence is common and gendered | Why it erupts in a particular case
:::
